ute_reply":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.131668Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>","text/markdown":"**What the record tells us (in plain language)**  \n- **Who is talking?**  \n  - **Source:** 192.168.1.5 (a private‑network host)  \n  - **Destination:** 10.0.0.7 (another private‑network host)  \n\n- **How are they talking?**  \n  - **Protocol:** TCP (port 443 coming from the source, port 8080 at the destination).  \n  - **Layer‑7 hint:** “L7_PROTO = 7” – in many NetFlow implementations this value maps to HTTP/HTTPS traffic.  \n\n- **How much traffic?**  \n  - **Inbound to the destination"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":9},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# === SAVE PoC ARTIFACT (persists as notebook output) ===\nwith open('/kaggle/working/poc_llm_explanation.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(response.choices[0].message.content)\nprint(\"poc_llm_explanation.md saved ✔\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.133811Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.134395Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.140211Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.134352Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-02T16:43:02.139278Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"poc_llm_explanation.md saved ✔\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":10},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Phase 0 Gate — every box ✔ before Phase 1\n[✔] Cell 1: Python, RAM, disk printed (no GPU — by design)  \n[✔] Cell 2: clone + uv sync completed with no errors  \n[✔] Cell 3: both CSVs found and staged (~550 MB visible in ls)  \n[✔] Cell 4: main.py --help printed  \n[✔] Cell 5: 1000 rows, ~53 columns  \n[✔] Cell 8: model list printed  \n[✔] Cells 9–10: LLM answered both prompts  \n[✔] Cell 11: artifact saved  \n[✔] Version saved (Save & Run All) + pushed to GitHub  \n[✔] README updated with Kaggle link","metadata":{}}]}